			"notes": "## ⚠️ 1.8.0 had a game-breaking bug on certain modpacks — this release fixes it\n\nWith some mod combinations, **simply putting an item into the Deposit slot froze the game outright.** No crash report, no error in `latest.log`, nothing to go on — the game just stopped responding.\n\nIt needed no misbehaving mod to trigger. Any pack containing a \"un-craft this back into planks\" style reverse recipe was enough: ordinary vanilla doors, boats and signs close the loop from the other side, so plain sticks, logs and stairs could all set it off. Underneath, the Deposit tab was re-walking a large slice of the recipe graph *on every rendered frame*, forever.\n\nSeparately, **four of the nine 1.8.0 downloads** (Forge 1.12.2, Forge 1.16.5, Forge 1.20.1 and NeoForge 1.21.1) were built minutes before the unlock sound was removed and shipped with it still in.\n\n**Both are fixed here.** Updating is a drop-in replacement — your catalog, teams and config carry over untouched, and there's nothing to re-research.\n\n## 🧊 The freeze\n\nThree compounding causes, all closed:\n\n* Threshold results are now cached properly, **including results resolved through a recipe cycle** — which 1.8.0 deliberately refused to cache, and that refusal is what turned every lookup into a full re-walk.\n* The Deposit tab and progress tooltips only recalculate when the item actually changes, instead of once per frame.\n* The recipe walk itself is now hard-bounded in both depth and total work, so no recipe graph — however pathological — can stall or stack-overflow the game.\n\n## 🩹 Other fixes\n\n* **Shift-click withdrew 64 of everything.** Shift-clicking in the Journey tab is meant to give a full stack, but \"full stack\" was hardcoded to 64 — so swords (which stack to 1) came out as 64 slots' worth, potions (16) likewise. Withdrawals now use each item's own stack limit, enforced server-side as well as client-side. Packs that raise stack limits get their raised limit.\n* **Team name overlapped the \"Journey Mode\" title.** They were drawn on the same line; they get a line each now.\n* **Stats tab per-mod list overflowed the panel**, running through the \"Latest:\" line and into the \"Inventory\" label below. The list scrolls now — mouse wheel, with a scrollbar when there's more to see — and long mod ids are trimmed to fit.\n* **Forge 1.19.2** was silently missing the unlock message and the team-name badge entirely; its sync handler had never been updated to the 1.8.0 payload. All nine versions now behave identically.\n* **Deposit All** printed one chat line per unlocked item on top of the batched on-screen message. Single summary line now.\n\n## 🚄 Performance & robustness\n\n* The Journey tab's search, the Stats tab and progress tooltips no longer rebuild their entire view every frame — noticeable on large catalogs, with no change in behaviour.\n* The data sync packet can no longer exceed Minecraft's payload limit on a very large catalog, which would have disconnected the client on every join.\n* Recipe-depth resolution can no longer overflow the stack on a pathological modded recipe graph.\n\n***\n\nAll nine loader/version combinations rebuilt from this commit: **Forge 1.12.2 / 1.16.5 / 1.19.2 / 1.20.1 · Fabric 1.16.5 / 1.19.2 / 1.20.1 / 1.21.1 · NeoForge 1.21.1**"
		},
